    "diagnosis": "<p>Sclerosing adenosis</p>",
    "title": "",
    "legend": "<p>Core biopsies show nodular sclerosing adenosis in two cores, where there are compressed epithelial cords and trabeculae amid a fibrocollagenous stroma.&nbsp; Myoepithelial cells, confirmed present on immunohistochemistry, show spindled shapes and merge with the stroma in areas.&nbsp; A vague nodularity is noted.</p>",
    "source": "<p>SGH Pathology</p>",
